            <ArticleTitle>Quadricuspid aortic valve without severe dysfunction despite advanced age.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>486-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 75-year-old woman who presented with stable angina and with a quadricuspid aortic valve, which consisted of 4 equal-sized leaflets that were diagnosed incidentally upon coronary angiography. Despite the patient's advanced age, the abnormal valve was functioning almost normally.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
